Z||000000||Predator||12-10-2000||02:36 PM||||I have finished installing the Design1Systems Stage II Turbo on my Fiero.<BR>When I tried to test it nothing happened when I tried to start it. It has power and all, but the engine does not turn over. I have a GM code reader so I used that and it comes back with the following code. 12 which means Diagnostic mode: no distributor signal to ECM System PASS. I have followed the directions to the letter so I am clueless to where this error code is leading. I don't want to bring this to a shop mainly because they are not going to understand all I did to install the Turbo anyway. If there is anybody in The Roswell, GA area that can help me with this I would appreciate a hand. I have been working on this for the past month, and now I can't even get it to turn over. It is frustrating to say the least to be finally done, and the car just sit there and look at you. Any help or advice will be greatly apppreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Predator||12-10-2000||02:47 PM||||Well I just found more information on Code 12 online. Please forgive my ignorance. 12 really doesn't mean anything at this stage from what I read other than the car is not running. Now I am really confused as to what the problem is. I guess I will start checing all the connections under the car starting with the starter and see whats what. Any help leading me in a direction will be appreciated. ||||reg||9
Z||000002||JohnnyK||12-10-2000||03:54 PM||||What all did you do to install the turbo? Did you disconnect the starter? Do you hear a click from the starter? You said the inside lights were working?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-10-2000||04:52 PM||||Predator, Is your P/N switch or clutch interlock switch connected? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Predator||12-10-2000||05:11 PM||||Clutch interlock switch.<BR>Where is that located.I had a little trouble with that before I started on the Turbo. Sometimes I would put the clutch in and it would not turn over. Then I would give it another push and it would crank.<BR>Starter.<BR>Yes I had to take disconnect the starter, remove the oil pan and lots of other stuff to install the Turbo. I double checked the connections to the starter and other stuff before I lowered the car, but I guess I will check it again. Thanks guys. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||12-10-2000||05:17 PM||||Uhhh  im like confused and stuff!!!!!<BR>Code 1-2 means normal operation for the stock v6 computer.<P>Haven't you checked your error codes before putting in the turbo?  I would think you saw 1-2 then as well.<P>Typically when doing the poor mans way (by reading the flashes of the check engine light)<BR>it does 1-2 at the beginning and at the end of the display sequence just to let you know the computer is OK.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 12-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||12-11-2000||07:49 PM||||Code 12 is an error, but it means No Reference Pulses. You'd expect that if the engine is not running.||||reg||1
